#   P2.x contains `success=true, error=<sentence>` -- a state no adapter over
#   {Ok, Error(d)} can represent at all. Counted over 200 elements the only
#   combinations present are (true, non-empty) and (false, non-empty); the
#   success state (true, empty) never occurs.

# M4: are the adapter's three states reachable from the payload set now?
#   Counted off DECODED values, not from the builder, and the state is read the
#   way an adapter would read it rather than from the fields directly.

  nested site (TaskDetailed.output, P2.2, 500 elements)
      Ok       (success, no error) 167
      Error    (error, no success) 167
      Invalid  (no child at all)   166
      IMPOSSIBLE (success AND error, which the message's own comment forbids) 0

  plain site (TaskSummary.error, P4.1, 200 elements)
      Error        (non-empty string)              67
      Ok OR Invalid (empty string -- INDISTINGUISHABLE) 133

#   The plain site's second row IS the finding: 133 elements carry a state the
#   wire form cannot tell apart, so an adapter must return one of two answers for
#   all of them and be wrong on the other. Before this the row was 0 and the
#   defect was unreachable.

